  "title": "Bonn intracranial EEG segments, sets C, D and E (Andrzejak et al. 2001)",
  "description": "Single-channel intracranial EEG segments (23.6 s each, 173.61 Hz) from five epilepsy patients in the Bonn dataset of Andrzejak et al. (2001). The release repackages sets C, D and E in BIDS: 300 segments covering seizure-free hippocampal recordings (opposite hemisphere and epileptogenic zone) and ictal activity. The samples are identical to the published source text files. The dataset supports nonlinear time-series analysis and seizure detection research.",
  "methods_description": "Segments were cut from continuous multichannel presurgical EEG recordings from depth and strip electrodes, after visual artifact inspection and a weak-stationarity check. Recordings used a 128-channel amplifier with an average common reference, 12-bit digitization at 173.61 Hz, and band-pass filtering at 0.53-40 Hz. The source text files were converted to BrainVision format without filtering, resampling or rescaling.",
